 {"version_id": "struct-05", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Normalize candidate patch fields and provide safe fallbacks at the patch-selection boundary", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "class CandidatePatch:\n    def __init__(self, id, patch, cleaned_patch, is_success_regression, is_success_patch):\n        self.id = id\n        self.patch = patch\n        self.cleaned_patch = cleaned_patch\n        self.is_success_regression = is_success_regression\n        self.is_success_patch = is_success_patch", "replace": "class CandidatePatch:\n    def __init__(self, id, patch, cleaned_patch, is_success_regression, is_success_patch):\n        self.id = id\n        self.patch = patch if isinstance(patch, str) else \"\"\n        self.cleaned_patch = cleaned_patch.strip() if isinstance(cleaned_patch, str) else self.patch\n        self.is_success_regression = bool(is_success_regression)\n        self.is_success_patch = bool(is"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.79, "execution_accuracy": 0.77, "output_integrity": 0.91}, "aggregate": 0.83, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.21}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.19}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": -0.005, "why": "Field normalization and fallbacks improve structural output safety, but silently converting malformed fields to empty patches can hide upstream errors and distort patch selection. That tradeoff lowers reasoning and execution reliability and does not address the difficult repository-level failures."}
 {"version_id": "struct-06", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Bias the selector toward minimal, behavior-preserving patches with explicit edge-case coverage", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "    init_prompt = f\"\"\"\\\n# ROLE: Act as an expert code evaluator. Given a codebase, an github issue and **{candidate_length} candidate patches** proposed by your colleagues, your responsibility is to **select the correct one** to solve the issue.", "replace": "    init_prompt = f\"\"\"\\\n# ROLE: Act as an expert code evaluator. Given a codebase, a GitHub issue, and **{candidate_length} candidate patches** proposed by your colleagues, select the correct implementation.\n\n# DECISION RULES:\nFirst reconstruct the issue's intended contract from the repository and tests. Select the smallest candidate that changes the owning abstraction, handles the reported edge c"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.91, "reasoning_soundness": 0.89, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.9}, "aggregate": 0.885, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.97}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.97}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.35}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.34}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.05, "why": "Reconstructing the intended contract, favoring minimal behavior-preserving changes, and requiring edge-case coverage gives the strongest combined improvement in selection quality and regression resistance. The minimality bias can occasionally under-select a broader necessary fix, limiting execution gains."}
 {"version_id": "struct-07", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Add a mandatory repository-diagnosis phase before editing, requiring the agent to map the issue to affected symbols, call paths, invariants, and existing tests before proposing a patch.", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"", "replace": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"\n\nBefore editing, perform a repository-specific diagnosis: identify the issue's observable contract, locate the owning implementation and all alternate call paths, inspect nearby tests and subclasses, and state the invariant that the patch must preserve. Do not edit until this diagnosis identifies the smallest complete change surface and the"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.91, "reasoning_soundness": 0.89, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.88, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.31}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.28}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 3x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.045, "why": "The mandatory symbol, call-path, invariant, and test mapping directly addresses repository-specific failures and improves diagnosis before implementation. It adds useful structure without changing patch execution or output handling, so gains are strongest on Django and Astropy while remaining modest elsewhere."}
+{"version_id": "struct-08", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Turn the existing edge-case reminder into an explicit behavior matrix covering normal, empty, null, boundary, subclass, alternate implementation, and backwards-compatibility paths.", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "For framework and scientific-library changes, check edge conditions explicitly: empty and null inputs, boundary values, subclass or alternate implementation paths, backwards-compatible defaults, error behavior, and interactions with existing public APIs. Preserve unrelated behavior and add or run regression coverage for each affected path.", "replace": "For framework and scientific-library changes, build a behavior matrix before editing: normal inputs; empty and null inputs; minimum, maximum, and boundary values; subclasses and alternate implementations; omitted versus explicit defaults; expected exceptions and messages; and interactions with existing public APIs. For every row, state whether behavior must remain unchanged or intentionally change"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.88, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8675, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.27}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.32}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0325, "why": "The behavior matrix improves explicit coverage of edge and compatibility paths, especially for scientific-library behavior like Astropy. It is somewhat broad and may add checklist overhead without ensuring correct diagnosis, so it is less effective than a repository-specific analysis for Django."}
